    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d793">

                <pb facs="0919" n="823" sameAs="frus:frus1921v02/pg823"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">861.48/1885</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Chief of the Division of Russian Affairs,
                        Department of State</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                            >Poole</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of State</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1921-12-27"><hi rendition="#italic">December 27,
                        1921</hi></date>.</dateline></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Mr. Secretary</hi>: The Russian Ambassador called
                    this morning “to express formally his deep appreciation and gratitude” for the
                    Russian relief measure which has just passed Congress.<anchor n="29"
                        xml:id="d793-f1"/> He said that he was convinced that it would assist the
                    recovery of Russia in every way.</p>
                <p>The Ambassador asked me to convey the foregoing to you, and expressed the hope
                    that you might find it convenient to convey it also to the President.</p>
                <p>Respectfully,</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">D. C. Poole</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d793-f1" n="29" xml:id="d793-f1-content">
                <p>See Executive Order No. 3601, Dec 24, <hi rendition="#italic">supra</hi>.</p>
            </note>
